Z||000000||Raydar||08-03-2000||08:14 PM||||Panasport wheels.<BR>Usta see them on MGs and Miatas. <BR>Come in a huge range of sizes. 10" to 17".<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FC15.jpg">  <BR> <A HREF="http://kspeed.com/pcomp.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://kspeed.com/proad.htm</A> <P>Wonder how they would look on a Fiero. It's not listed, but I'll bet they're available in a 5x100 pattern.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>"Some mornings, it just isn't worth<BR>chewing through the restraints."<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 08-03-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||08-03-2000||08:32 PM||||I had/have a set.. had 8psi in a set of Nitto NT555Rs and the bead broke at Commerce and trashed both rear wheels.. still have both fronts.. Panasport superlights.. 8.3lbs a piece 14x7 5x100 38mm offset. you can get them from <A HREF="http://www.panasport.com" TARGET=_blank>www.panasport.com</A>  or <A HREF="http://www.paulspruell.com" TARGET=_blank>www.paulspruell.com</A>  that where i got mine.. $183 each. another great superlight wheel is made by Fikse.. but they are ONLY special order and start at about $600 each  <A HREF="http://www.fikse.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fikse.com</A> ||||reg||1
